=EF=BB=BFI've gotten into a jam now.

For an image to work nicely on a Zynq processor, it needs to load the FPGA=
=20
with useful stuff, and it also needs to adapt the (SPL) bootloader to=20
configure the clocks etcetera at boot.

The FPGA image recipe yields "ps7_init.[ch]" files which must be compiled i=
nto=20
u-boot, and which are to be created usin Xilinx tools.

For now, I've invented a "virtual/xilinx-sdk" package that can be provided =
by=20
the FPGA recipe, and u-boot-spl that DEPENDS on it. In the machine or local=
=20
config, one can set PREFERRED_PROVIDER_virtual/xilinx-sdk=3D"package" and t=
hus=20
pick the FPGA design that will be responsible for the bootloader.

My problem now is that the FPGA configuration is actually something that th=
e=20
"image" decides upon, and multiple configurations can be used for a single=
=20
machine (great all programmable hardware) because the FPGA part can impleme=
nt=20
just about anything (and switch that at runtime too).

Is there a way to propagate a PREFERRED_PROVIDER via the image?

Or shoud I move in another direction and consider a slightly differently=20
configured FPGA as a totally new MACHINE? Maybe use MACHINE_CLASS to join t=
hem?

I'm interested in your ideas, opinions, tricks, etc...


--=20
